  "question": {
    "text": "Wavelength of light used in an optical instrument are $\\lambda_1=4000 Å$ and $\\lambda_2=5000 Å$, then ratio of their respective resolving powers (corresponding to $\\lambda_1$ and $\\lambda_2$ ) is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n16 : 25\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n9 : 1\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n4 : 5\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n5 : 4",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Resolving power $\\alpha(1 / \\lambda)$. Hence, $\\frac{(\\text { R.P })_1}{(\\text { R.P })_2}=\\frac{\\lambda_2}{\\lambda_1}=\\frac{5}{4}$"
  }
